{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #723 [status: falsifiable; formalized: yes]. If there is a finite projective plane of order $n$ then must $n$ be a prime power?\n\nA finite projective plane of order $n$ is a collection of subsets of $\\{1,\\ldots,n^2+n+1\\}$ of size $n+1$ such that every pair of elements is contained in exactly one set. Current best: This conjecture has been proved for $n\\leq 11$, but it is open whether there exists a projective plane of order $12$. Prize: no. Tags: combinatorics."},"claim_id":"vcl_1fb073b398afc40aad9ce79ba3a75f34898811be24a6da551e36ae252ee82743","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:723","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_9d11b2829a90d809","object_root":"sha256:76dea2178975a08dce0cde8a9c3ef1506d5d0078545b3d8101f453e2f96d95ef","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:723"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}